# A global package-manager install in a Dockerfile without a version installs
# whatever is "latest" at build time: two builds of the same Dockerfile get
# different tools, and a compromised release lands silently. Pin every package
# (`npm install -g pnpm@12.21.0 yarn@1.22.22`).
#
# A repo-local pin guard (one script in one repo) only protects that repo;
# as a rule every repo with keur gets it.
#
# HOW the regex works without lookaround (RE2): after `-g`/`--global`, zero or
# more PINNED tokens (`name@version`, scoped `@s/n@v` too) are consumed, then a
# BARE token (no `@` after its first character) must follow and be followed by
# whitespace or end of line. A pinned token cannot be read as bare because it is
# followed by `@`, not whitespace. A line continuation `\` or `&&` is not a token
# start, so `pnpm@1 yarn@1 \` is clean.
#
# `^[^#]*` keeps a Dockerfile comment (`# RUN npm install -g x`) out: skip_comments
# does not know Dockerfile comments, so the pattern itself refuses a leading `#`.
#
# Limits (80% fit): flags between `-g` and the packages (`-g --unsafe-perm x`)
# and the `npm i x -g` order are not seen (false negative, never a false positive).
#
# @see docs/rules-authoring.md (RE2: no lookaround), ADR-026 (maturity).
id: DK-PIN-001
ilities: [integrity, reliability-maturity]
maturity: 2
title: Unpinned global npm/pnpm/yarn install in a Dockerfile
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
action: block
skip_comments: true
target:
  filenames: Dockerfile Dockerfile.dev Dockerfile.prod
  extensions: .dockerfile
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/
patterns:
  - regex: ^[^#]*\b(npm|pnpm)\s+(install|i|add)\s+(-g|--global)\s+(@?[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*@[^\s\\&;|]+\s+)*@?[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*(\s|$)
    message: "global install without a version: pin every package (pkg@x.y.z) so the image build is reproducible"
  - regex: ^[^#]*\byarn\s+global\s+add\s+(@?[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*@[^\s\\&;|]+\s+)*@?[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*(\s|$)
    message: "yarn global add without a version: pin every package (pkg@x.y.z) so the image build is reproducible"
fix: "Add an exact version to each package, e.g. RUN npm install -g pnpm@12.21.0 yarn@1.22.22, and let Renovate bump it."
